    xpBounty: 70,
    paradigm: "Dynamic Programming Running Prefix Reset",
    coreConcept: "Optimal contiguous subarray sum tracking in strictly linear time",
    timeComplexity: "O(N) Strict Single-Pass Time",
    spaceComplexity: "O(1) Constant Auxiliary Memory",
    description: "Optimal contiguous subarray sum tracking in strictly linear time (Dynamic Programming Running Prefix Reset) \u2014 Time: O(N) Strict Single-Pass Time.",
    theory: "#### Problem Definition\nGiven an array $A$ of $N$ integers (which may include negative numbers), find the maximum possible sum of a non-empty contiguous subarray:\n$$\\max_{0 \\le l \\le r < N} \\sum_{i=l}^r A[i]$$\nand recover the starting and ending indices $(l, r)$ of this optimal subsegment.\n\n#### Dynamic Programming Formulation\nLet $\\text{current\\_sum}[i]$ denote the maximum sum of a contiguous subarray ending at index $i$:\nAt step $i$, there are only two choices:\n1. Extend the previous subarray: $\\text{current\\_sum}[i - 1] + A[i]$\n2. Start a completely fresh subarray at index $i$: $A[i]$\n\nThus:\n$$\\text{current\\_sum}[i] = \\max\\Big(A[i], \\ \\text{current\\_sum}[i - 1] + A[i]\\Big)$$\n* If $\\text{current\\_sum}[i - 1] < 0$, it is always detrimental to extend it; we restart the subarray at index $i$.\n\nThe global maximum subsegment sum across the entire array is simply:\n$$\\text{max\\_sum} = \\max_{0 \\le i < N} \\text{current\\_sum}[i]$$\n\n#### Space Compression to $O(1)$\nBecause $\\text{current\\_sum}[i]$ depends only on $\\text{current\\_sum}[i - 1]$, we do not need an array! We maintain a single running scalar `cur_sum` and update `max_sum` in real time.\n\n#### Subsegment Boundary Reconstruction\nTo extract the exact indices $(l, r)$:\n* Keep a running candidate start pointer `cur_start`.\n* When `cur_sum < 0`, reset `cur_sum = 0` and advance `cur_start = i + 1`.\n* Whenever `cur_sum > max_sum`, update `best_l = cur_start` and `best_r = i`.",
    code: "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass KadaneAlgorithm {\npublic:\n    struct SubsegmentResult {\n        long long max_sum;\n        int start_idx;\n        int end_idx;\n    };\n\n    KadaneAlgorithm() {}\n\n    // 1. Kadane's Algorithm with Subsegment Range Extraction in O(N):\n    static SubsegmentResult solve(const vector<int>& a) {\n        int n = a.size();\n        if (n == 0) return {0, -1, -1};\n\n        long long max_so_far = a[0];\n        long long cur_sum = a[0];\n\n        int best_l = 0, best_r = 0;\n        int cur_l = 0;\n\n        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n            // 2. Decide whether to extend existing subarray or start anew:\n            if (cur_sum + a[i] < a[i]) {\n                cur_sum = a[i];\n                cur_l = i;\n            } else {\n                cur_sum += a[i];\n            }\n\n            // 3. Update global maximum and boundaries:\n            if (cur_sum > max_so_far) {\n                max_so_far = cur_sum;\n                best_l = cur_l;\n                best_r = i;\n            }\n        }\n\n        return {max_so_far, best_l, best_r};\n    }\n};",
